led snake-polynomial which oscillates most between ±µ, but it turned out\n\nto be a rather difﬁcult question.\n\nIn the previous paper, we proved that this is true in the case of symmetric majorant provided\n\nthe snake-polynomial has a positive Chebyshev expansion. In this paper, we show that that the\n\nconjecture is valid under the condition of positive expansion only, hence for non-symmetric\n\nmajorants as well.\n\n1 Introduction\n\nThis paper continues our studies in [7] and it is dealing with the problem of estimating the max-\n\nnorm k p(k)k of the k-th derivative of an algebraic polynomial p of degree n under restriction\n\n|p(x)| ≤ µ(x), x ∈[−1,1],\n\nwhere µ is a non-negative majorant. We want to ﬁnd for which majorants µ the supremum of\n\nk p(k)k is attained by the so-called snake-polynomial ω µ which oscillates most between ±µ, namely\n\nby the polynomial of degree n that satisﬁes the following conditions\n\na)|ω µ(x)| ≤ µ(x), b)ω µ(τ∗\n\ni) = (−1)i µ(τ∗\n\ni), i = 0,...,n.\n\n(This is an analogue of the Chebyshev polynomial T n for µ≡1.) Actually, we are interested in\n\nthose µ that provide the same supremum for k p(k)k under the weaker assumption\n\n|p(x)| ≤ µ(x), x ∈δ∗= (τ∗\n\ni)n\n\ni=0,\n\nwhere δ∗is the set of oscillation points of ω µ. These two problems are generalizations of the\n\nclassical results for µ≡1 of Markov [4] and of Dufﬁn-Schaeffer [2], respectively.\n\nFig. 1. Markov inequality with a majorant µ:\n\n|p| ≤ µ, k p(k)k → sup\n\nFig. 2. Dufﬁn-Schaeffer inequality with a majorant µ:\n\n|p|δ∗≤ |µ|δ∗,k p(k)k → sup\n\n1\n\nProblem 1.1 (Markov inequality with a majorant) For n, k ∈N, and a majorant µ≥0, ﬁnd\n\nM k,µ := sup\n\n|p(x)|≤µ(x)k p(k)k(1.1)\n\nProblem 1.2 (Dufﬁn–Schaeffer inequality with a majorant) For n, k ∈N, and a majorant µ≥0,\n\nﬁnd\n\nD∗\n\nk,µ := sup\n\n|p|δ∗≤|µ|δ∗k p(k)k(1.2)\n\nIn these notation, results of Markov [4] and Dufﬁn–Schaeffer [2] read:\nTheorem 1.3 ([7]) Let ω(k−1)\n\nµ∈Ω. Then\n\nM k,µ =D∗\n\nk,µ =ω(k)\n\nµ